  "metaDescription": "MPR RI has rescheduled the plenary session for the election and inauguration of the new vice president to December 11, 2026, following public feedback.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has officially rescheduled the vice president election plenary session to December 11, 2026.",
    "Chairman Ahmad Muzani stated that the delay follows feedback regarding procedural rules and the need for careful deliberation to avoid ambiguity.",
    "President Prabowo Subianto is expected to submit two vice-presidential candidates for the MPR to review as part of the formal selection process."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) is currently managing the process to fill the vacant vice presidency following the departure of Gibran Rakabuming Raka. Following initial discussions and external feedback regarding the integrity of the election rules, MPR leadership recently confirmed that the plenary session for the selection and subsequent inauguration of the new vice president will now take place on December 11, 2026. MPR Chairman Ahmad Muzani emphasized that the body is prioritizing caution to prevent potential legal or interpretive conflicts during the voting process. President Prabowo Subianto is required to propose two candidates for the position. The MPR has established specific working groups and verification teams to oversee the submission and vetting of these candidates. Leadership members recently met with the presidential palace to communicate the revised schedule and discuss the administrative procedures necessary for a consistent and orderly transition.",
